  "application_type_full": "Full planning permission",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The property would be not suitable for conversion to a House in Multiple Occupation as it would not be located within an area with good access to public transportation and convenient walking distance of town centre facilities, and the original floor space of the existing flat would be less than 130 square metres. Furthermore, the applicant has failed to demonstrate that the development together with other similar developments in the area would not result in cumulative harm to the character and residential amenity in the area. The proposal is therefore unacceptable in principle, contrary to Local Plan policy SC10, CC1 and CC2, and the Houses in Multiple Occupation SPD.",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposal, by reason of bedroom sizes, poor outlook, insufficient details of daylight levels and inadequate and lack of external amenity area, would fail to provide an acceptable standard of accommodation for future occupants and would be overdevelopment of the site. The proposed is therefore contrary to Local Plan policies SC5 and SC10, and the aims and the Houses in Multiple Occupation SPD.",
    "Reason : 3 - The application has failed to provide adequate cycle parking provision. In the absence of sufficient details and given the low PTAL rating for the site, the scheme has failed to demonstrate that the proposal would have an acceptable impact on the local highway and not result in additional excessive parking stress on the roads surrounding the development. The proposed development is therefore contrary to Local Plan policy EC2, SC10 and the Houses in Multiple Occupation SPD. ",
    "Reason : 4 - The application has failed to provide sufficient information to demonstrate that satisfactory waste and recycling storage and collection arrangements can be achieved. The proposed development is therefore contrary to Local Plan policies EQ7, SC10 and the Houses in Multiple Occupation SPD.",
    "Reason : 5 - On account of insufficient fire safety information, the application fails to comply with the minimum requirements of London Policy D12a."
  ],
